fresh-editor for the Debian archive
===================================

This directory is a debian/ directory for building Fresh the way the Debian
archive would. It is separate from the repository's own debian/, which
builds the .deb attached to upstream releases from crates.io with every
default feature.

How it differs from an upstream build:

 * Rust crates come from Debian's librust-*-dev packages, offline, through
   dh-cargo's cargo wrapper; the upstream Cargo.lock is not used.
 * The JS engine is Debian's QuickJS (libquickjs, linked statically, hence
   Static-Built-Using) through Fresh's own binding, selected with
   RUSTFLAGS="--cfg fresh_js_system", instead of rquickjs.
 * Plugin TypeScript is compiled by Debian's esbuild at run time (cached
   under ~/.cache/fresh/esbuild), instead of the oxc crates; hence
   Depends: esbuild.
 * Features: runtime, plugins, embed-plugins. No tree-sitter (its JavaScript,
   TypeScript and Templ grammars are not packaged), no http/self-update
   (update checks, telemetry, self-update), no gui.

The manifests still name the crates Debian lacks, as optional or
other-target dependencies, and cargo resolves those too. debian/rules runs
`scripts/debian.py patch-manifests`, which rewrites the manifests so the
workspace resolves from /usr/share/cargo/registry alone (and `clean` puts
the originals back). It prints each dependency it drops and why.

The librust-*-dev Build-Depends are generated from Debian testing's index:

    scripts/debian.py packages --control Packages.xz

and `scripts/debian.py check Packages.xz` checks that the archive can supply
every dependency of the build. Upstream CI runs the check, and the
`Debian package` workflow (.github/workflows/debian-package.yml) builds
this package from a fresh orig tarball on every pull request.
Releases attach its output beside the main .deb, under names the updater
and install.sh never pick: fresh-editor_<ver>-1_<arch>.debian-testing.deb
(amd64, arm64) and fresh-editor_<ver>-1.debian-testing-source.tar.gz (the
.dsc with its orig and debian tarballs). The package version follows the
workspace version in Cargo.toml.

To build from a checkout:

    git archive --prefix=fresh-editor-0.5.2/ HEAD | xz > ../fresh-editor_0.5.2.orig.tar.xz
    rm -rf debian && cp -r packaging/debian debian
    sudo apt-get build-dep ./
    dpkg-buildpackage -us -uc

Copyright
---------

debian/copyright was audited against the whole source tree: licensecheck
over every file, and the git history of every file that could be
third-party (grammars, queries, themes, fonts, images, fixtures). To
re-check after upstream changes, in the unpacked source:

    lrc          # licenserecon: compares debian/copyright with licensecheck

debian/lrc.config lists, with reasons, the files that only mention a license.
